The page compares this chain with 3CX and tj-actions, and contrasts this stealer with the CHAINDROP / keyv watcher. The four topics are the page's related defense topics.
notes:
The page links three other kill chains, and four defense topics.

It compares this chain with the 3CX / X_TRADER compromise of 2023, which also began on an employee's personal computer, and with the tj-actions/changed-files compromise of 2025, where a stolen token moved existing version tags. It contrasts this stealer with the watcher in the CHAINDROP / keyv worm: none of the four sources describes a revocation trigger or destructive behavior in this stealer.

The page's related defense topics are CI/CD security, Git and version control, non-human identity, and incident response. CI/CD stands for continuous integration and continuous delivery.
